==In the manga==
===Pokémon Adventures===
[[File:Battle Girl Hex Maniac Adventures.png|thumb|200px|A Battle Girl in the {{MangaArc|Emerald}} of Pokémon Adventures]]
===={{MangaArc|Emerald}}====
In ''[[PS319|Verily Vanquishing Vileplume I]]'', a Battle Girl named Cyndy (Yukari in the [[Chuang Yi]] translation) was seen battling {{tc|Bug Catcher}} James in the [[Battle Dome]]. Though the outcome of that battle was unknown, Cyndy was known to have lost a match at some point, thus eliminating her from the tournament.

===={{MangaArc|HeartGold & SoulSilver}}====
A Battle Girl was amongst the people visiting the {{safari|Johto}} in ''[[PS446|Weavile Wobbles But It Won't Fall Down]]''.

===={{MangaArc|Diamond & Pearl}}====
A Battle Girl was one of the contestants who partook in the [[Super Contest]] in ''[[PS351|Perturbed by Pachirisu]]'', where she was instructed by 2 wealthy individuals to sabotage {{adv|Platinum}}'s [[Dance Competition]]. Nevertheless, Platinum was able to win the [[Rank (Contest)|Normal Rank]] {{OBP|Cool|condition}}ness {{pkmn|Contest}}.

===={{MangaArc|Platinum}}====
In ''[[PS418|Deprogramming Porygon-Z]]'', a Battle Girl was seen waiting in a line to challenge the [[Battle Castle]]. Another Battle Girl briefly appeared with her {{p|Meditite}} at the {{Gdis|Battle Frontier|IV}} in ''[[PS351|Perturbed by Pachirisu]]''.

